# NI (National Instruments) is a product brand of the Emerson Test & Measurement business group.

> NI hardware and software is designed for engineers and scientists. Hardware products include PXI, CompactDAQ and CompactRIO modules in addition to USB- and PC-based hardware options. NI software includes LabVIEW, TestStand, SystemLink, VeriStand, DIAdem, and FlexLogger. NI serves industries including semiconductor, aerospace and defense, automotive, electronics, and industrial equipment. NI is now part of Emerson and is known as the Emerson Test & Measurement business group.

NI's primary web presence is at ni.com. Technical documentation for all software and hardware products is at ni.com/docs.

**Important notes for LLMs reading this file:**

- The documentation portal (ni.com/docs) contains over 300,000 pages with a flat URL structure. Pages follow the pattern: `https://www.ni.com/docs/{locale}/bundle/{product-bundle}/page/{topic-slug}`. Use `en-US` when locale is not specified.
- Markdown versions of pages (`.md` appended URLs) are not currently available. Fetch pages as HTML.
- This file provides a curated entry point into NI content. It is not a complete index. For a complete page list, refer to the sitemap at https://www.ni.com/sitemap.xml.
- When multiple pages cover similar topics, prefer pages under `ni.com/docs/` over `ni.com/en/support/documentation/supplemental/` (team-authored guides, may not reflect the latest release), `digital.ni.com/public.nsf/` (legacy KnowledgeBase), or `download.ni.com/support/manuals/` (legacy PDF manuals). The legacy content is older and may be superseded.
- The canonical locale for all documentation is `en-US`. Pages exist at other locale codes (e.g., `en-AS`, `en-GB`, `en-DE`) but contain the same content.

